1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Global Opportunity Intelligence.
A local desk that keeps the public source next to the claim.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:34,002
The overview is stored data.
Counts come from the database, not from a target.

3
00:00:34,002 --> 00:00:50,106
Twenty-seven companies are stored. Ninety-two signals were collected.
Sixty-five of those signals are not linked to a company.

4
00:00:50,106 --> 00:01:04,230
Historical score, business signal, technical evidence, and freelance fit
stay in separate columns.

5
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:16,303
Six leads are in review. The search is narrowed to Stitch.ai.
Opening the row does not change it.

6
00:01:16,303 --> 00:01:30,335
The historical score is still 76.
That is the old composite, not the three-score result.

7
00:01:30,335 --> 00:01:50,367
Business signal is 70. Technical evidence is 25. Freelance fit is 0.
A launch is not yet a freelance job.

8
00:01:50,367 --> 00:02:04,421
Quality assurance rejected the old service line.
The company stays in review. Nothing was sent.

9
00:02:04,421 --> 00:02:14,421
This is the existing Switch room.
These messages were already stored. Nothing was typed or sent.

10
00:02:14,421 --> 00:02:24,421
The orchestrator and the specialist agents share one thread.
Switch is the collaboration layer.

11
00:02:24,421 --> 00:02:48,464
GOIP stores the same room activity. The seven agents are members.
These rows were already stored.

12
00:02:48,464 --> 00:03:02,511
Settings shows which integrations are configured.
The secret values are not on this page.

13
00:03:02,511 --> 00:03:12,513
The older high-priority labels are still the first scorer.
They have not been rewritten.

14
00:03:12,513 --> 00:03:20,263
The operator uses the web application.
FastAPI serves that page and the API.

15
00:03:20,263 --> 00:03:28,013
Discovery code fetches Hacker News, TechCrunch, GitHub,
and one Crawl4AI query.

16
00:03:28,013 --> 00:03:35,763
Research and qualification call OpenRouter.
Switch is not the model provider.

17
00:03:35,763 --> 00:03:43,513
Seven agents are members of one room.
The orchestrator is the one a person addresses.

18
00:03:43,513 --> 00:03:51,263
The runtime posts stage messages into Switch
and reads the replies.

19
00:03:51,263 --> 00:03:59,013
PostgreSQL stores companies, signals, evaluations,
reviews, and those messages.

20
00:03:59,013 --> 00:04:06,763
Mattermost is attached by Switch as the human composer.
GOIP does not call it.

21
00:04:06,763 --> 00:04:14,513
A solid arrow is HTTP. A dashed arrow is a room message.
The brown arrow is a database write.

22
00:04:14,513 --> 00:04:30,513
GOIP keeps the source next to the claim.
Switch is the room where that work is visible. No outreach was sent.

